    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass with a clean build. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did to unify `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`:\n\n**Field definition (OpenAPI \u2192 generated DTO)** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`\n- Replaced the `customerCode` schema with `memberId`, and removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit`.\n\n**Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Renamed the `customerCode` field/column (`customer_code`) to `memberId` (`member_id`) with its getter/setter.\n\n**Database schemas** \u2014 `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`\n- Renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` and bumped the varchar length to 32 to hold the longer id.\n\n**Mapper** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.java`\n- Removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and the `checkDigit(Owner)` method. `memberId` now maps straight through (stored value); `fiscalYear` is unchanged.\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- Replaced `generateCustomerCode` with `generateMemberId`, building `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region from postcode/city, 2-digit fiscal year from the business-day-adjusted registration date, the existing SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-hex `HASH8`, and a Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Added `fiscalYearSuffix` and `luhnCheckDigit` helpers.\n- Collision de-duplication now runs against existing owners' `memberId`.\n- The audit line and structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` (via `primaryIdentifier`), and no longer log `customerCode` or `membershipNumber`.\n\nBehaviour confirmed by the acceptance suite: `memberId` starts with the region and contains the exact `HASH8` (Cp32/Cp56), the old fields are gone (Cp09/Cp14/Cp16/Cp31), de-dup keeps ids unique (Cp41), `fiscalYear` and `ownerSegment` are unchanged (Cp48/Cp55), and the audit line/event reference the memberId (Cp21/Cp43/Cp53).",
